        "problem": "Find the imaginary part of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}8+\\text{i} & 3-4\\text{i} \\\\ 9 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}8+\\text{i} & 3-4\\text{i} \\\\ 9 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8+\\text{i} & 3-4\\text{i} \\\\ 9+0\\text{i} & 0+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Im}(A)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
