        "knowledge_point_id": "66d82fa3-d576-5c42-9dca-4e1b76473424",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Range of a Transformed Reciprocal Function",
        "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=\\frac{3}{1-x}+2?$",
        "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=2.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14094369/assets/c9178fda4e7479b7f351dbb193547d795c6a55cab2fed7e0d076cfd104e62d39.png)",
